---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DEMO_CHARACTERS } from "../../data/legends-demo";
import { href } from "../../lib/href";

const rows = [...DEMO_CHARACTERS].sort((a, b) => b.overall - a.overall || a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
---
<Base title="Rankings" description="A Brick Legends leaderboard layout with demonstration data only." section="legends">
  <p class="eyebrow">Community rankings</p>
  <h1 class="lede">Leaderboards, before the votes</h1>
  <p class="notice">No accounts, votes, or popularity counts exist. The table is a layout preview sorted by the fictional overall score from rule bl-rarity-1. That score is not a community rating. Categories that need votes stay empty on purpose.</p>
  <div class="rank-tabs" aria-label="Ranking categories">
    <span class="chip">Highest rated · no votes</span>
    <span class="chip">Most creative · no jury</span>
    <span class="chip">Community favorites · no votes</span>
    <span class="chip">Most popular this year · no votes</span>
    <span class="chip">Legendary collection · not open</span>
    <span class="chip">Hall of fame · no inductees</span>
  </div>
  <table>
    <caption>Demonstration characters. Not a ranking of real creators.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Character</th>
        <th>Fictional overall</th>
        <th>Rarity label</th>
        <th>Community rank</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {rows.map((character) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{character.name}<br /><span class="quiet">{character.creator} · {character.id}</span></td>
          <td>{character.overall}</td>
          <td>{character.rarity}</td>
          <td>Not available</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Voting, if it is added later, has to live on a server that can enforce one eligible vote, slow down bots, accept reports, and record the formula in public. This static site cannot do that safely. <a href={href("brick-legends/policies/")}>See the requirements</a>.</p>
</Base>
